of the companies that you are investing in.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:46.500
Generally speaking, there's two views on this. One&nbsp;
view is if you focus on ESG, you're going to get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:53.760
an inferior return because the most profitable&nbsp;
companies may not adhere to whatever is sort of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:59.640
like in vogue at the time in terms of adhering&nbsp;
to environmental and social issues. So it's a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:04.680
perfectly fine way to invest, but you're just&nbsp;
going to have a lower return. The the increasing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:10.860
counterpoint is that over the medium to long term,&nbsp;
the most profitable companies will be the ones&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:15.960
that are environmentally and socially conscious,&nbsp;
so that actually it's the best of both worlds.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:19.380
You're doing a good thing morally and ethically,&nbsp;
and you're also going to get the highest return.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:26.820
Honestly, my view on this is not a morality view.&nbsp;
It's informed my but my by my views generally on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:31.200
